# Reference quarantine

`*.Reference` modules (today: `Hom.Reference` in the separate
**`quantum-reference`** package) hold densify / basis-sum / dynamic-LA
oracles for QuickCheck and probes.

## Do not

- Import any `*.Reference` module from production code under `src/` that is
  exposed by the main `quantum` library (`Fusion.*`, `Hom.*` except Reference,
  `Symmetry.CG.SU2`, …).
- Re-export densify / `fMultBlock` / `denseFMove*` from production CG or Hom
  modules.
- Put dynamic `Numeric.LinearAlgebra` densify back into `Symmetry.CG.SU2`.

## Do

- Keep CG densify only in `Hom.Reference` (`quantum-reference` package).
- Production SU(2) F scalars: `Symmetry.CG.SixJ.su2FAmpTJ` via `FusionData.fSymbol`.
- Tests / scripts that need oracles: `build-depends: quantum-reference`.

## Compiling vs correct

If a production call site “needs” densify, stop and co-plan — that is a missing
morphism or a misplaced oracle, not a reason to weaken the quarantine.
